1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,771
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,279
<i>From this day forward,</i>

6
00:00:29,362 --> 00:00:31,990
<i>you will address me by my real name.</i>

7
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,450
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

8
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:35,118
[Robert] <i>This is not your arena</i>
<i>anymore, Governor.</i>

9
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:37,245
<i>Mateo Ruiz is officially the governor now.</i>

10
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:39,330
<i>Don't lose yourself</i>
<i>in fighting a lost game</i>

11
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:42,083
<i>or else it'll be harder for you</i>
<i>to restore your name.</i>

12
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,710
[Lily] <i>Diego and I will be the bridges</i>

13
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:46,963
<i>connecting you to the new government.</i>

14
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:48,548
[Emilia] <i>Even though we're</i>
<i>no longer in power,</i>

15
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:51,009
<i>I can still make your life miserable.</i>

16
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:55,638
<i>Just accept that both you</i>
<i>and your family have lost.</i>

17
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:56,848
<i>What's more important to you?</i>

18
00:00:56,931 --> 00:00:58,558
<i>Becoming the queen of Ardiente,</i>

19
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:01,102
<i>or discovering your mom's identity?</i>

20
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:03,980
<i>Both. I want to be the queen of Ardiente</i>

21
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:10,028
<i>and have acting governor Mateo Ruiz</i>
<i>at my beck and call.</i>

22
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:14,074
<i>-Someone wants to see you.</i>
<i>-Who?</i>

23
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,909
<i>Red Dragon.</i>

24
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:19,704
<i>I am now the consultant</i>
<i>of Governor Mateo Ruiz.</i>

25
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:23,124
<i>I will help him with decisions</i>
<i>that affect this town.</i>

26
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,876
<i>Governor, is this a joke?!</i>

27
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,211
<i>Whether you like it or not,</i>

28
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:28,505
<i>I get to decide for the governor.</i>

29
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:31,174
[Mercedes] <i>Madam, here's</i>
<i>the research you ordered.</i>

30
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:40,475
Governor, could you give me a second?

31
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:43,561
Next time, talk to my secretary
if you want an appointment.

32
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:45,772
Oh, I'm sorry about that, Governor.

33
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:49,859
I thought that, being your consultant,
I could go straight to you.

34
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:53,696
And I thought also that, you know,
we should work closely together

35
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:54,948
for the people of Ardiente.

36
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:56,825
Okay, fine. What is it? Make it quick.

37
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:57,867
I'm in a hurry, okay?

38
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:00,203
[exhales] So, you really do
like it fast, huh?

39
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:01,621
Don't waste my time.

40
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:03,081
Okay.

41
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:06,376
First off, I'd like to thank you
for appointing me

42
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:08,503
as your consultant.
Can I call you "Mateo"?

43
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:11,172
Since it's just the two of us
here right now.

44
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,967
Tell me the truth.

45
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:16,594
Does my father have anything
to do with your decision?

46
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:18,638
No.

47
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:20,765
Hmm…

48
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:22,809
Then, who?

49
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:25,186
You know, I'm just wondering.

50
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:28,064
Because, if I remember it correctly,

51
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,775
you rejected me before,
even if I offered you

52
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:33,153
something more than
what your wife could give you.

53
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:39,492
Emilia, I chose you because I like you.

54
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:42,745
In fact, I've been eyeing you
for a long time.

55
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:48,084
But you're an Ardiente, and I'm a Ruiz.

56
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:51,462
World War III will erupt
if we mess around.

57
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,674
But, who knows?

58
00:02:55,758 --> 00:03:00,138
Behind closed doors, maybe we
could work something out?

59
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:07,520
Careful, Mateo. Don't mix
business with pleasure.

60
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,856
We're both married.

61
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:12,483
So, don't give in to temptation.

62
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:15,153
Excuse me.

63
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:19,115
[unsettling music playing]

64
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:21,826
[sighs]

65
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:30,335
I heard Emilia's happy
with her new position.

66
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:33,713
She reminds me of you, madam.

67
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:37,634
Hungry for power.

68
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:42,430
And like you, Emilia could have it all.

69
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:49,354
[suspenseful music playing]

70
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:53,942
Hi, Papa.

71
00:03:54,025 --> 00:03:55,026
Hmm.

72
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:57,403
Hello there.

73
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,072
My daughter, please, please.

74
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:03,618
You look a little tired.
How was your first day at work?

75
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:05,453
Um, tiring, Papa.

76
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:08,414
Uh… Have you had dinner already?

77
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:09,958
Yeah, I'm good.

78
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:13,586
Would you like a piece
of cake or ice cream?

79
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,004
No, thanks, Papa.

80
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:17,757
But I think you need
something from me. What is it?

81
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:22,262
Oh, come on. Isn't that a little too much?

82
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:26,015
Haven't you gotten used
to our love-hate relationship?

83
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:28,935
We will always have our petty quarrels.

84
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:31,980
But, where the rubber hits the road,

85
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:34,774
we will be there for each other.

86
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:39,279
At the end of the day, my dear,
we will always be family.

87
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:40,905
I know, Papa.

88
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:44,409
I just can't believe you're
being so nice to me right now.

89
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:47,370
-So, what do you need?
-No… Actually…

90
00:04:47,453 --> 00:04:51,708
Actually, I just have this
very little favor to ask of you.

91
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:55,295
I knew you needed something.
Okay, what is it?

92
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:58,381
-Look, it's a very small favor.
-I knew it.

93
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:03,886
Now that you're working
for this Mateo Ruiz…

94
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,555
-[Emilia] Yes?
-[Julio] I want you to sabotage

95
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:08,975
all of his projects, lead him to his ruin.

96
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:12,687
That way, I can become governor again.

97
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:16,357
Seriously, Papa?
Aren't you still under trial?

98
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,443
You know what? Instead of
serving at the capitol,

99
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:19,986
you'll end up serving time in prison.

100
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:22,572
[Julio] Come on, Emilia.

101
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:26,951
How many times have cases like
these been filed against me?

102
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:31,748
Have you ever seen me
spend a day in prison?

103
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,249
I've never been imprisoned,

104
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:36,544
and the day will never come
that I will be.

105
00:05:37,795 --> 00:05:42,967
Just make sure that by the end
of my 90-day suspension,

106
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:46,429
Mateo Ruiz will have been
kicked out of my office.

107
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:50,516
-I'll think about it, Papa.
-What?!

108
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:52,018
Think about--

109
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,854
Emilia, this is your obligation!

110
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:57,065
It's your obligation to this family

111
00:05:57,148 --> 00:06:01,360
to make sure that we will remain in power!

112
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:04,322
And what is it
that you want me to do, Papa?

113
00:06:05,281 --> 00:06:06,324
It's very simple.

114
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,410
You're the only one who can do this

115
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:11,704
because you're the only woman among us.

116
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:14,874
You're a woman. And he's a man.

117
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:19,754
You're a very attractive woman.
I'm sure he'll give in to you.

118
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:23,883
Papa! You're going to use me
as a prostitute?

119
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:26,344
No way! I'm not doing it!

120
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:31,265
Emilia, you don't have to go that far.

121
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:36,270
Men are like dogs.

122
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:37,647
[imitates dog barking]

123
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:41,776
A few pats on the head,
a little caress here and there,

124
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:44,487
and they're all yours.

125
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:49,534
We all have sacrifices
to make for this family.

126
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:53,955
-I know.
-[Julio] Good. You see?

127
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:58,709
I knew you'd understand
and you'd get the point.

128
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:04,882
Goodbye, Mr. Mateo Ruiz.

129
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:06,008
[Julio chuckles]

130
00:07:09,387 --> 00:07:14,100
I'm sure it wasn't an Ardiente
who influenced Governor Ruiz

131
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,602
because they don't have any power left.

132
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,729
They only have their name to hold on to.

133
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,941
The Ruiz I know isn't like that.

134
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,944
He's not afraid of any Ardiente.

135
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:28,531
The Ardientes are his enemies.

136
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:32,160
There's no way he'd form
an alliance with them.

137
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:37,248
But then, we all know how politics works.

138
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:41,169
Your enemy today
could be your ally tomorrow.

139
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:42,295
[scoffs]

140
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:46,632
What if he just wanted to be governor

141
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:50,011
so he could fulfill
his own personal ambitions?

142
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:52,889
[Diego] If that's the case,

143
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:55,808
we shouldn't have trusted him so easily.

144
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:59,729
Diego, it's not our fault.

145
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:05,568
We needed Governor Ruiz to take
Julio down, and we succeeded.

146
00:08:07,445 --> 00:08:09,822
But we still have to face the facts.

147
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:14,368
The world never runs out of evil people.

148
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:16,704
And soon enough we'll find out

149
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:20,166
who's manipulating Governor Ruiz.

150
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:25,296
One thing's for sure,
it's not an Ardiente.

151
00:08:27,673 --> 00:08:28,966
I'm sure of it.

152
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:30,968
Raul, you're here.

153
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:34,597
[scoffs]

154
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:36,849
Did I hear that right?

155
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:38,809
Huh?

156
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:40,895
You're working for that fool?

157
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,438
Fool? Who?

158
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:45,191
Isn't it obvious?
Who else are you working for?

159
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:46,943
I'm talking about the governor.

160
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:48,319
-Is it true?
-Here we go…

161
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:50,446
What's your connection with him?
Why did he hire you

162
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,948
as his consultant? What's going on?

163
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:53,658
Raul, what's up with you?

164
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:55,952
I'm tired. I want to rest.

165
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:58,287
Wait. I'm not done talking to you.

166
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:03,584
I'm asking you. What's going on? Tell me!

167
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:05,294
What's there for me to tell you?

168
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:07,004
Did something happen between you?

169
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:11,425
I can't believe you and Papa
think the same thing about me!

170
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:13,052
He hired me as his consultant

171
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:15,930
because I am the former governor
and mayor of this town,

172
00:09:16,013 --> 00:09:17,682
which means I can help him.

173
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:19,308
If he has a hidden agenda,

174
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,561
-that's not my problem anymore!
-Yes, it is!

175
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:23,646
That should be your concern
because we're married!

176
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:27,191
Unless you're doing all this
on purpose just to mess with me!

177
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:30,695
Just because I let that thing between you

178
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:32,071
-and the Jaguar slide…
-What?

179
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:33,864
Now, you've got another guy lined up?

180
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:36,325
And you even chose that Mateo!
Am I nothing to you?!

181
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,744
You checked my phone, didn't you?

182
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:40,746
I'm changing my password right now!

183
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:43,207
See? If you aren't guilty,
you wouldn't do that!

184
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:48,546
You know what, Raul? We are nothing alike.

185
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,715
You give in to any woman
who so much as smiles at you.

186
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:55,678
Now you know how painful it was
for me every time you cheated!

187
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:59,056
Now, you know how it feels,
so deal with it!

188
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:03,936
[footsteps fading]

189
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:07,690
[sighs]

190
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:15,865
Hmm…

191
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:19,785
[chuckles]

192
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:28,544
Oh, Emilia. It's hard being beautiful.

193
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:33,799
Today marks the beginning
of the fulfillment of my dreams.

194
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:36,385
Ever since I was a kid,

195
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:40,348
I've been longing
for a prosperous Ardiente.

196
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:46,395
That was also my father's dream
before he passed away.

197
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:50,691
This will be the site
for the media complex,

198
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:53,277
which will provide education and jobs

199
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:55,780
to all the citizens of Ardiente.

200
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:58,824
[applause]

201
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:04,538
[suspenseful music playing]

202
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:06,666
Stop!

203
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:10,294
[suspenseful music playing]

204
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:15,549
What are you doing here?

205
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,968
I have an order from the office
of the governor

206
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:20,763
to stop this event because
you're lacking some permits.

207
00:11:20,846 --> 00:11:22,306
Also, you didn't get my approval.

208
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:24,850
I highly doubt that, Emilia.
This isn't illegal!

209
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:26,310
We have the necessary permits,

210
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:29,605
so you can't stop me
from fulfilling my plans!

211
00:11:29,688 --> 00:11:32,942
And which city official did you
sleep with to earn your permit?

212
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:37,613
Well, Emilia, I'm not like you.
We went through due process.

213
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:41,242
I have a cease and desist order
from the office of the governor.

214
00:11:41,325 --> 00:11:42,952
I don't care about that.

215
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:45,704
We didn't ask your office for funds.

216
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:50,960
Just so you know, this project
is 100% funded by Aguas Realty.

217
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:54,672
Furthermore, I bought this space.

218
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:56,424
And that means you're trespassing!

219
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:57,675
But you have to stop

220
00:11:57,758 --> 00:12:00,094
this little project of yours, Lily Cruz,

221
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:03,264
until we settle this dispute in court.

222
00:12:03,347 --> 00:12:04,473
Do you have a title?

223
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:07,476
I do. Want me to slap it in your face?

224
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,437
Well, I also have a title
to slap your face with!

225
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,980
-Go ahead!
-Huh?

226
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:17,111
Don't test me, Emilia.

227
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,654
That is fake.

228
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:21,323
Yours is the fake one! Just like you!

229
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:23,117
In case you didn't hear me right…

230
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:27,288
You need to leave!
You have to get out of here!

231
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:36,464
Just to repeat myself!
I bought this space!

232
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:39,842
Therefore, you're trespassing! Get out!

233
00:12:39,925 --> 00:12:42,553
Get out! Get out!

234
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:45,973
Did you hear me?

235
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:47,975
Just try and come back here, Emilia.

236
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:51,312
I'll make sure you'll go deaf!

237
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:53,606
Get out!

238
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,570
-That's right!
-Serves them right.

239
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:05,034
Sorry about that.

240
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:08,621
I just don't want anyone
maltreating any of you

241
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:11,207
because this project is
for everyone's benefit.

242
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,876
-[applause]
-Thank you.

243
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:21,967
Just call me tomorrow,

244
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,720
or visit me in my office
at around 4:00 p.m.

245
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:26,472
-Mateo Ruiz.
-Thank you.

246
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:28,349
-Thank you.
-Hold on. Sir, wait.

247
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:30,267
I just need to talk to him.
Let me speak with him.

248
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,852
-Let me talk to him.
-It's fine. Let him talk.

249
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:32,895
What is it?

250
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:35,397
What are you doing with my wife? Huh?

251
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:38,234
Why did you hire her as your consultant?

252
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,486
You're planning to do something
with her, aren't you?

253
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,363
I have no idea what you're talking about.

254
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:43,864
You know exactly what I'm talking about!

255
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:45,991
-You're making a pass at my wife!
-Sir, calm down.

256
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,161
You know who I am.

257
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,788
You know what I'm capable of doing!

258
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:52,665
You've got a lot of nerve!

259
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:55,543
Tell me. What can you possibly do to me?

260
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,461
You're no longer the Raul Torillo

261
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:59,213
that people feared.

262
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,423
No one respects you anymore.

263
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:06,679
Even your wife mocks you because
you're nothing but a loser!

264
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:10,224
Loser, huh?

265
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:14,478
[suspenseful music playing]

266
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:28,450
Attorney, I can't let
Emilia delay this project.

267
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:30,494
This is for the townspeople.

268
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:34,957
The people will lose
if we let this happen.

269
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,626
Her papers are fabricated.

270
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,879
But nonetheless, she can cause problems

271
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,089
and delay the project
with her dirty tactics.

272
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:45,634
That's Emilia's plan.
Even if we win in court,

273
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:48,178
she'll be more than happy
if she can obstruct us.

274
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:53,726
No. We won't let it reach court.

275
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:59,690
Attorney, what we're going to do
is start a signature campaign

276
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:01,901
to show the government

277
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:03,777
the amount of support
this project is receiving.

278
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:06,697
That way, they'll stop Emilia.

279
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,533
This project is for the townspeople,

280
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,493
so we'll let their voices be heard.

281
00:15:18,876 --> 00:15:20,836
What signature campaign, Papa?

282
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:23,505
That is what I heard.

283
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:26,216
And if they get enough support,

284
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:30,429
Mateo will be forced to favor them.

285
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:34,350
You can't let this happen, Emilia.

286
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:36,060
You have to do something about it.

287
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:43,651
-Miss Loring. How's it going?
-[Loring] Yes?

288
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,736
-Have you gathered many signatures?
-Distribute this to everyone.

289
00:15:45,819 --> 00:15:47,321
-I think this is enough.
-Here. Take these.

290
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:48,489
But we have more areas

291
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:50,115
-to go to.
-Make everyone sign.

292
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:52,409
-[Loring] Mm-hmm.
-Remember, everyone,

293
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,912
we need one million signatures.

294
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:56,830
We'll pass this to the local government

295
00:15:56,914 --> 00:16:00,834
to let them know how important
Lily Cruz's project is to us.

296
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:04,254
We won't lose to the Ardientes.

297
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:06,799
You know very well,
just as the Ardientes do,

298
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:09,134
that we can take them on! Right?

299
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:10,511
-That's right!
-Right!

300
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:14,139
You heard her, everyone.
Don't give up! Fight!

301
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,976
[townspeople] Fight!

302
00:16:22,439 --> 00:16:25,234
They were able to gather more
than a million signatures

303
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:26,527
in less than a week.

304
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:29,071
Their campaign was very effective.

305
00:16:29,154 --> 00:16:30,906
They even went viral.

306
00:16:31,448 --> 00:16:34,868
Governor Ruiz was forced
to let the project happen.

307
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:41,250
Madam, Lily Cruz has the people
of Ardiente behind her.

308
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:44,586
It's about time we let her know

309
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:46,922
that you're not to be messed with.

310
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:51,176
[suspenseful music playing]

311
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,304
[tires screeching]

312
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:58,726
[suspenseful music playing]

313
00:17:06,775 --> 00:17:09,695
Who are you? What do you want?

314
00:17:09,778 --> 00:17:12,031
[suspenseful music playing]

315
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:18,120
[men grunting]

316
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:25,544
[men groaning, grunting]

317
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:29,173
[suspenseful music playing]

318
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:53,614
Jaguar? What is this?

319
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:55,866
[in distorted voice] Emilia Ardiente.

320
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:01,497
I just want you to know that she's mine.

321
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:06,960
I don't care about Emilia.
She's all yours.

322
00:18:09,838 --> 00:18:11,799
[in distorted voice]
You better make sure of that.

323
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:15,594
Because if you're lying,
I'll come for you.

324
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:20,140
[Mateo groans]

325
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:26,855
[suspenseful music playing]

326
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:46,917
[sensual music playing]

327
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:05,227
[sensual music playing]

328
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:16,029
<i>Ma'am, hold on.</i>

329
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:17,531
[sensual music playing]

330
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,917
Jepoy?

331
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,252
Anna.

332
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:33,005
It's okay. Just wait for me outside.

333
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:38,802
Why are you here?

334
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:41,013
You didn't tell me you were coming.

335
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:43,765
It's late, and it's dangerous outside.

336
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:45,934
I'll drop you home.

337
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:48,729
It's okay. Lily gave me
bodyguards, remember?

338
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:54,610
Anna, you actually trust them
more than me?

339
00:19:56,069 --> 00:20:01,867
[soft tense music playing]

340
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:12,127
-[line ringing]
-[phone ringing]

341
00:20:17,674 --> 00:20:19,551
Yes, I trust them

342
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:21,261
because I'm the only one they're guarding.

343
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:22,387
-While you--
-Anna.

344
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:28,727
[sets phone down]

345
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:33,523
Anna, wait. Anna.

346
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:38,153
[romantic music playing]

347
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:52,918
[romantic music playing]

348
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:11,895
Listen.

349
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:15,148
Why don't you tell
your bodyguards to go for now?

350
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:17,943
I'll be your bodyguard tonight.

351
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:21,738
[romantic music playing]

352
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:33,041
It's all right, Jepoy. Maybe next time.

353
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:36,336
You should go to her.
Don't keep a lady waiting.

354
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,879
Anna… Anna.

355
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:44,052
Mateo, I thought we already
decided to reject

356
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:46,972
whatever project Lily Cruz starts up!

357
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:48,932
Why did you approve of her project?!

358
00:21:49,224 --> 00:21:51,184
Lily got the people's support.

359
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:52,894
Also, it called the attention
of the media.

360
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:56,189
If we rejected the project,
it'll be held against us.

361
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:59,776
So what? Emilia Ardiente is your backer.

362
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,069
That should be enough reason

363
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:03,196
for you to stand your ground
against Lily Cruz!

364
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:06,074
Emilia, I've made my decision,
and my decision is final, okay?

365
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:07,784
So, stop with the bickering!

366
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,244
No! This isn't over!

367
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:12,581
You think I don't notice
you disregarding me?

368
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,792
You wouldn't want to mess with me, Mateo.

369
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:21,882
[Mateo] I just don't want
any issues, Emilia.

370
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:25,343
You know, ever since you started
working for me,

371
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:29,097
I've had so many rivals.

372
00:22:29,639 --> 00:22:34,519
So, if you want this partnership
to last, tell off your allies.

373
00:22:35,062 --> 00:22:37,647
My allies? Who are you talking about?

374
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:40,233
Why don't you ask Jaguar?

375
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:48,241
To Aguas Realty. Cheers!

376
00:22:48,325 --> 00:22:50,494
Cheers!

377
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:54,289
[Paterno] Congratulations.

378
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:55,582
Lily.

379
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:58,168
-Mr. Paterno.
-Congratulations.

380
00:22:58,251 --> 00:23:00,629
Your dream project
is finally in the works.

381
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:03,423
Thank you. How was Europe?

382
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:05,425
Uh… Melissa and I?

383
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:07,135
Yeah, we had a great time in Europe.

384
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:09,721
Well, please send my regards to your wife.

385
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:10,931
Of course.

386
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:13,600
And, Mr. Paterno, thank you very much

387
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:17,395
for helping and supporting
my little pet project.

388
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:19,231
Uh, you know what?

389
00:23:19,898 --> 00:23:22,192
As long as it doesn't affect
our business negatively…

390
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:27,572
I'm all for your charitable
endeavors. Count on it.

391
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:28,824
Thank you.

392
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:33,995
Well, Mr. Paterno, our company
is blessed with so much success.

393
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:36,873
So, it's our duty
to give back to the community.

394
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:39,876
-All right.
-Again, thank you.

395
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,254
And congratulations.

396
00:23:42,420 --> 00:23:43,839
-[glasses clinking]
-Thank you.

397
00:23:44,714 --> 00:23:47,300
[tense music playing]

398
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:55,517
Jaguar!

399
00:23:57,602 --> 00:24:00,522
You know, I hate you! I really hate you!

400
00:24:00,605 --> 00:24:01,773
[in distorted voice] Leave us for now.

401
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,233
Yes, boss.

402
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:09,364
Why did you do that, huh?!
Why did you attack Mateo?

403
00:24:09,447 --> 00:24:11,324
Are you trying to ruin my plans?!

404
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,535
What's up with you, Emilia?

405
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:16,288
What's up with me, huh?

406
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:19,708
You're ruining my plans
for Governor Mateo Ruiz!

407
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:21,501
So, why did you attack him?

408
00:24:22,002 --> 00:24:24,546
I just don't want you
getting close to that man.

409
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:26,173
I knew it all along!

410
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:28,550
You're so heartless, you know that?

411
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:32,220
All you want is power, money,
and control over Ardiente.

412
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:34,931
But, you don't care about me. I knew it!

413
00:24:35,348 --> 00:24:36,766
That's enough, Emilia!

414
00:24:37,934 --> 00:24:40,187
I don't want you getting any close to him.

415
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:43,190
Because I'm jealous.

416
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:50,197
I think you better leave.

417
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,075
[chuckles]

418
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:57,621
So, Jaguar's in love with me now?

419
00:25:04,502 --> 00:25:07,047
[mellow music playing]

420
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:10,383
[water running]

421
00:25:13,428 --> 00:25:16,806
<i>Should I give this to her?</i>
<i>Are they sweet enough?</i>

422
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:19,184
<i>What if she gets the wrong message?</i>

423
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,770
<i>What if she thinks I'm courting her?</i>

424
00:25:23,021 --> 00:25:24,773
<i>No, what if I get turned down?</i>

425
00:25:29,527 --> 00:25:30,528
Damian!

426
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:33,365
The food's almost ready.

427
00:25:33,448 --> 00:25:34,407
We'll be eating in a bit.

428
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:35,533
All right.

429
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:37,994
What's that?

430
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:39,287
-That thing you're holding.
-Uh… This?

431
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:43,833
Um… They're mangoes.
I can't finish them all.

432
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:45,502
I picked them earlier.

433
00:25:46,419 --> 00:25:48,922
Um… Do you want some?

434
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:51,925
Oh, sorry, Damian!

435
00:25:52,467 --> 00:25:55,887
I was at the market earlier,
and I already bought mangoes.

436
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:59,599
Is that so?

437
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:02,727
No worries. I'll just give these
to someone else, okay?

438
00:26:04,145 --> 00:26:05,480
No, wait!

439
00:26:07,274 --> 00:26:08,525
Let me have them.

440
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:10,944
Really?

441
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:14,906
Yeah, let's just give mine away, instead.

442
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:16,074
[chuckles]

443
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,701
Thank you, Damian.

444
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:22,372
-Check them out.
-Okay.

445
00:26:23,832 --> 00:26:26,668
-Look. See how ripe they are?
-They are.

446
00:26:26,751 --> 00:26:27,711
They're really sweet.

447
00:26:28,336 --> 00:26:29,254
Thanks.

448
00:26:37,512 --> 00:26:43,643
Whether it's against Ivy Aguas
or Lily Cruz, you still lost!

449
00:26:44,227 --> 00:26:49,899
What's the point of becoming
that vile vermin's consultant

450
00:26:49,983 --> 00:26:52,444
if you can't even influence
any of his decisions?!

451
00:26:53,111 --> 00:26:54,696
You're useless!

452
00:26:59,576 --> 00:27:01,077
Ma'am, sir! It's Mr. Arnaldo.

453
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:03,288
Why? What happened to my grandson?

454
00:27:03,747 --> 00:27:06,499
Please, come upstairs
and see for yourself.

455
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:08,460
[suspenseful music playing]

456
00:27:18,053 --> 00:27:19,179
[Julio] Arnaldo?

457
00:27:19,512 --> 00:27:20,930
-Arnaldo?
-Arnaldo?

458
00:27:21,681 --> 00:27:22,849
Arnaldo?

459
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:26,561
Amen.

460
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:31,232
[dramatic music playing]

461
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:41,159
Uh…

462
00:27:42,118 --> 00:27:43,244
Who are you?

463
00:27:43,661 --> 00:27:45,705
[tense music playing]

464
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:05,100
[line ringing]

465
00:28:05,183 --> 00:28:06,267
Anna.

466
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:07,977
<i>Anna, I'm here outside.</i>

467
00:28:08,478 --> 00:28:11,898
I was hoping we could go
see Lily together.

468
00:28:11,981 --> 00:28:14,192
Are you sure you don't have other plans?

469
00:28:14,275 --> 00:28:15,944
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

470
00:28:16,986 --> 00:28:19,864
I know it's a special day
for you and Lily,

471
00:28:19,948 --> 00:28:22,367
so I figured
I could be your bodyguard today.

472
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:23,952
<i>Just to make it up to you.</i>

473
00:28:24,244 --> 00:28:26,121
All right. I'm on my way out.

474
00:28:26,621 --> 00:28:27,872
Okay. I'll wait.

475
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:37,674
[suspenseful music playing]

476
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:39,759
Come with us.

477
00:28:39,843 --> 00:28:42,095
What--Wait!

478
00:28:42,178 --> 00:28:43,555
Go ahead and try!

479
00:28:43,638 --> 00:28:44,597
-[grunts]
-[crackling sound]

480
00:28:44,681 --> 00:28:45,682
[goon] Let's go!

481
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:49,769
[goon 2] Hurry up!

482
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:52,605
[suspenseful music playing]

483
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:01,114
Lily, I'll just be with Loring, okay?

484
00:29:01,197 --> 00:29:02,115
-Sure, Mom.
-Excuse me.

485
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:03,283
-Okay.
-Excuse me.

486
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:06,286
Okay.

487
00:29:07,203 --> 00:29:10,415
This building's construction
was halted due to lack of funds,

488
00:29:10,498 --> 00:29:14,377
but since Aguas Realty owns this now,

489
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:18,465
the media complex for the
residents of Poblacion, Ardiente

490
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:21,217
can now be erected.

491
00:29:21,301 --> 00:29:22,969
Your help made all this possible.

492
00:29:23,052 --> 00:29:24,679
So thank you very much.

493
00:29:25,972 --> 00:29:27,015
Um…

494
00:29:27,807 --> 00:29:29,976
[suspenseful music playing]

495
00:29:40,111 --> 00:29:41,154
Um…

496
00:29:43,072 --> 00:29:45,074
Mr. Paterno, let's go?

497
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:48,828
You take the lead so we can
begin the building inspection.

498
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:54,709
[suspenseful music playing]

499
00:29:58,755 --> 00:30:00,423
-Good day, ma'am.
-Good day.

500
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:03,092
[suspenseful music playing]

501
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:21,486
[suspenseful music playing]

502
00:30:37,585 --> 00:30:40,213
[suspenseful music playing]

503
00:30:55,937 --> 00:30:58,147
[suspenseful music playing]

504
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:16,457
[Lily] And the--

505
00:31:18,751 --> 00:31:21,004
Um… Miss?

506
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:25,758
[suspenseful music playing]

507
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:31,347
Diego, do you know that woman?

508
00:31:31,764 --> 00:31:32,891
Doesn't she work here?

509
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:36,519
I think so. But all alone?

510
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:42,483
Diego, please gather everyone outside.

511
00:31:42,984 --> 00:31:44,068
All right.

512
00:31:45,528 --> 00:31:48,531
[suspenseful music playing]

513
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,833
Mister, have you seen Jepoy?

514
00:31:58,917 --> 00:32:00,043
No, ma'am.

515
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:04,172
Hold on. Let me go and check.

516
00:32:04,255 --> 00:32:07,675
Never mind. We're running late
for Lily's event.

517
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:08,801
[bodyguard] All right.

518
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:13,097
[suspenseful music playing]

519
00:32:23,399 --> 00:32:24,359
Watch your step.

520
00:32:28,279 --> 00:32:32,659
Uh, Diego, have you seen
my mom and Miss Loring?

521
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:34,035
Uh, they're inside.

522
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:37,288
Oh, there they are.

523
00:32:37,705 --> 00:32:38,665
[Lily] Okay, good.

524
00:32:38,748 --> 00:32:41,250
Okay. I think um… that's it for today.

525
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:44,921
[beeping sound]

526
00:32:46,047 --> 00:32:50,051
[explosions]

527
00:32:50,134 --> 00:32:51,844
[screaming]

528
00:32:51,928 --> 00:32:54,722
[explosions]

529
00:33:00,436 --> 00:33:01,479
Ivy.

530
00:33:03,231 --> 00:33:04,607
[Diego] Auntie? Auntie.

531
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:06,567
[Ivy] Mom! Mom!

532
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:08,361
-[Diego] Auntie.
-Mom.

533
00:33:08,778 --> 00:33:10,113
[groans] Uncle.

534
00:33:10,196 --> 00:33:12,156
[whimpering]

535
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:16,703
[suspenseful music playing]

536
00:33:21,749 --> 00:33:23,126
Mom, I think you should go home now.

537
00:33:23,209 --> 00:33:25,378
Go home, and call Anna and Jepoy.

538
00:33:25,461 --> 00:33:28,339
Check on them, and let me know
if they're okay. Okay?

539
00:33:28,423 --> 00:33:31,134
-Go! Get the car ready!
-What about you, Lily?

540
00:33:31,217 --> 00:33:32,385
Come with me. This place isn't safe.

541
00:33:32,468 --> 00:33:34,762
I'm sorry, Mom, but I can't
leave my employees here.

542
00:33:34,846 --> 00:33:36,556
Uncle, you go ahead. We'll catch up.

543
00:33:36,639 --> 00:33:37,557
-Come with us!
-Auntie.

544
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:38,808
-Get moving! Come on!
-[Diego] Go, Uncle.

545
00:33:38,891 --> 00:33:40,268
-Go ahead. We'll be fine.
-Get the car ready!

546
00:33:40,351 --> 00:33:41,436
Go, Auntie. I'll take care of Lily.

547
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:43,646
-Please. Go, Nanny, Uncle.
-Mom, I'll call you.

548
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:44,939
[Loring] Why don't you just come with us?

549
00:33:45,023 --> 00:33:46,816
Mr. Paterno, are you okay?
Please, call an ambulance.

550
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:49,527
Hurry! Check if everyone's okay!

551
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:54,157
-[line ringing]
-Hello?

552
00:33:54,657 --> 00:33:58,077
-[tense music playing]
-[fire crackling]

553
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:08,838
[suspenseful music playing]

554
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:26,105
[suspenseful music playing]

555
00:34:43,498 --> 00:34:44,999
[reporter] <i>Six condominium buildings</i>

556
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,751
<i>were simultaneously bombed today,</i>

557
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,127
<i>as well as a media complex</i>
<i>being constructed</i>

558
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:49,253
<i>under Aguas Realty.</i>

559
00:34:49,337 --> 00:34:51,464
<i>All the buildings are notably</i>
<i>owned by Lily Cruz,</i>

560
00:34:51,547 --> 00:34:53,508
<i>formerly known as Ivy Aguas.</i>

561
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:56,761
<i>Terrorists are thought</i>
<i>to be behind the bombings.</i>

562
00:34:57,261 --> 00:35:00,515
<i>Stay tuned for news updates.</i>

563
00:35:01,724 --> 00:35:04,102
[suspenseful music playing]

564
00:35:14,153 --> 00:35:16,614
<i>Six condominium buildings</i>
<i>and a media complex</i>

565
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:19,659
<i>owned by Aguas Realty</i>
<i>were bombed earlier this morning</i>

566
00:35:19,742 --> 00:35:22,036
<i>in what could be</i>
<i>the deadliest terrorist attack</i>

567
00:35:22,120 --> 00:35:23,412
<i>in recent memory.</i>

568
00:35:23,579 --> 00:35:25,081
<i>Please stay tuned for more updates…</i>

569
00:35:25,164 --> 00:35:28,751
It's clear you were the target
of those bombings.

570
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:32,380
Who could've done this? Who?

571
00:35:37,468 --> 00:35:39,011
Did you receive the money?

572
00:35:39,428 --> 00:35:41,389
-Yes, ma'am.
-[Mercedes] <i>Good.</i>

573
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:44,684
That is our thank-you gift
for your successful mission.

574
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:50,398
[suspenseful music playing]

575
00:35:57,947 --> 00:36:01,409
Wait… What's… Hey! Stop!

576
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:04,579
I said stop! Where am I?!

577
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:07,206
-She's here. Let's go.
-Who's here?

578
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:09,876
Hey! Where am I?

579
00:36:11,794 --> 00:36:15,798
Where are you going?
Let me go! I'm talking to you!

580
00:36:20,303 --> 00:36:21,345
[grunts]

581
00:36:22,763 --> 00:36:25,474
Well, hello, Madrigal.

582
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:28,519
Ma'am? Ma'am, what's going on?!

583
00:36:29,937 --> 00:36:35,484
Well, what Natalie wants, Natalie gets.

584
00:36:40,114 --> 00:36:42,283
You didn't have to do this, ma'am.

585
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:45,411
Three men had to bring me here.

586
00:36:45,912 --> 00:36:47,330
-I'm sorry.
-They even tasered me.

587
00:36:47,413 --> 00:36:50,249
Oh. I'm sorry about that.

588
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:56,047
But I finally have you where I want you.

589
00:36:58,466 --> 00:37:00,176
So, are you going to
make this harder for me?

590
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:03,262
-Mm?
-Ma'am…

591
00:37:03,512 --> 00:37:06,015
Ma'am, wait.

592
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:08,059
Ma'am…

593
00:37:08,684 --> 00:37:09,644
[grunts]

594
00:37:10,353 --> 00:37:11,437
Ma'am…

595
00:37:20,529 --> 00:37:22,949
We are facing dozens of lawsuits.

596
00:37:23,574 --> 00:37:25,993
We'll have to cover the medical expenses,

597
00:37:26,077 --> 00:37:28,329
as well as compensation for the injured!

598
00:37:29,997 --> 00:37:32,667
Take note, we'll spend millions

599
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:35,086
just to pay for freaking damages!

600
00:37:38,422 --> 00:37:40,216
The company might lose billions.

601
00:37:41,467 --> 00:37:42,468
That's it.

602
00:37:42,551 --> 00:37:46,430
Aguas Realty is done for,
and it's all your fault.

603
00:37:48,015 --> 00:37:49,767
With all the enemies you've made,

604
00:37:50,393 --> 00:37:52,019
they're after us now.

605
00:37:52,103 --> 00:37:54,814
[tense music playing]

606
00:38:09,036 --> 00:38:10,121
Yes.

607
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:15,334
This is my fault.

608
00:38:16,711 --> 00:38:18,838
But as the CEO of this company,

609
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:24,885
I promise you, while I'm here,

610
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:29,515
Aguas Realty will not go under.

611
00:38:30,766 --> 00:38:34,270
What we need to do now
is to help each other.

612
00:38:38,774 --> 00:38:42,737
And we need to help all the victims.

613
00:38:43,738 --> 00:38:47,533
[tense music playing]

614
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:04,091
[tense music playing]

615
00:39:13,100 --> 00:39:15,728
Arnaldo is suffering
from retrograde amnesia.

616
00:39:15,811 --> 00:39:17,605
It has a chance of occurring in patients

617
00:39:17,688 --> 00:39:19,231
who woke up from a coma,

618
00:39:19,315 --> 00:39:21,525
coming from a catatonic state.

619
00:39:21,609 --> 00:39:23,152
Let's give him time.

620
00:39:23,444 --> 00:39:27,239
Eventually, he will regain
all his old memories.

621
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:29,075
Arnaldo.

622
00:39:31,327 --> 00:39:33,120
Do you remember me?

623
00:39:35,915 --> 00:39:37,208
I'm your grandfather.

624
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:42,171
I was the one who raised and molded you…

625
00:39:42,671 --> 00:39:45,091
to be the mayor of this town.

626
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:48,469
[Emilia] Yes, Arnaldo.
You were the mayor before.

627
00:39:48,552 --> 00:39:50,096
You were supposed to run for governor,

628
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:53,015
but you fell into a coma.

629
00:39:55,351 --> 00:39:57,978
[Julio] You are an Ardiente, Arnaldo.

630
00:39:58,312 --> 00:40:02,650
The Ardiente family is the wealthiest…

631
00:40:03,567 --> 00:40:06,987
and most powerful clan in this province.

632
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:11,158
Truth is, this place
was even named after us.

633
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,535
And you…

634
00:40:13,702 --> 00:40:16,497
You are the heir to my throne.

635
00:40:18,874 --> 00:40:21,419
Arnaldo, I'm your mother.

636
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:25,256
And I'm your father, Arnaldo.

637
00:40:30,761 --> 00:40:31,720
Grandpa.

638
00:40:35,349 --> 00:40:36,600
-Mom.
-Mm-hmm.

639
00:40:40,354 --> 00:40:41,397
Dad.

640
00:40:47,486 --> 00:40:50,698
So, do you remember us now?

641
00:40:54,243 --> 00:40:55,286
Not really.

642
00:40:57,872 --> 00:41:00,541
But… But I want to thank you all.

643
00:41:00,624 --> 00:41:05,087
Because, since I've been
unstable and unconscious

644
00:41:05,171 --> 00:41:06,213
for so long…

645
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:10,926
I can only imagine how long
you suffered and waited.

646
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:13,804
So, thank you very much
for not leaving me.

647
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:17,641
May I ask what happened to me?

648
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:19,435
You were shot in the head.

649
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:22,521
I was shot in the head? How…

650
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:26,567
Yes. We'll tell you the story,
but not now.

651
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:28,068
-Right.
-In bits and pieces.

652
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:29,236
So you won't be shocked.

653
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,447
Yes. You better get some rest for now.

654
00:41:31,530 --> 00:41:35,284
Did someone really shoot me?
Do I have enemies?

655
00:41:35,951 --> 00:41:38,204
Arnaldo, I think, for now,

656
00:41:38,787 --> 00:41:41,373
we should just be thankful
that you're finally awake.

657
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:43,209
Uh…

658
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:48,631
We can now carry on with
the plans we've made together.

659
00:41:50,216 --> 00:41:54,678
All right. Again, thank you very much.

660
00:41:55,971 --> 00:41:57,139
[exhales]

661
00:41:59,099 --> 00:42:02,144
Please bless my family. Guide them always.

662
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:03,229
What did he say?

663
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:06,732
This I pray always. Forever.

664
00:42:06,815 --> 00:42:08,651
I think the boy is just tired.

665
00:42:08,943 --> 00:42:12,029
We should give him some time to rest.

666
00:42:12,821 --> 00:42:15,199
Doc, please let him rest for now.

667
00:42:18,577 --> 00:42:21,622
[indistinct chatter]

668
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:28,587
[Arnaldo] Thank you.

669
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:36,428
Based on our investigations,

670
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:40,891
Aguas Realty did not fall short
in our security measures

671
00:42:40,975 --> 00:42:43,978
within any of our establishments.

672
00:42:44,061 --> 00:42:46,772
This series of bombings were a deliberate

673
00:42:46,855 --> 00:42:49,066
and deadly act of terrorism

674
00:42:49,149 --> 00:42:53,279
to hurt, kill, and instill fear.

675
00:42:53,362 --> 00:42:56,198
<i>They may have destroyed our buildings,</i>

676
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:58,701
<i>but never our spirit.</i>

677
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:03,622
<i>They've only made Aguas Realty stronger.</i>

678
00:43:04,081 --> 00:43:05,332
<i>We will rise again,</i>

679
00:43:05,416 --> 00:43:11,005
<i>and we will be a symbol</i>
<i>of strength, courage, and hope.</i>

680
00:43:11,797 --> 00:43:14,675
<i>We will help all of the victims,</i>

681
00:43:15,342 --> 00:43:20,055
<i>and we will hunt down</i>
<i>whoever was behind this.</i>

682
00:43:23,267 --> 00:43:27,479
This is an attack on justice, freedom,

683
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:30,232
and the future of our country.

684
00:43:30,566 --> 00:43:33,569
<i>That is why, I, Lily Cruz,</i>

685
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:41,201
<i>and Aguas Realty, humbly ask</i>
<i>for your help and support.</i>

686
00:43:44,079 --> 00:43:46,498
We need to show them…

687
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:48,751
<i>that we are not afraid,</i>

688
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:52,129
<i>and we will not let them bring us down</i>

689
00:43:53,088 --> 00:43:55,924
<i>because we're all united</i>
<i>in this fight.</i>

690
00:43:56,008 --> 00:43:58,719
[applause]

691
00:44:07,353 --> 00:44:10,981
This is fantastic! Just great, you know?

692
00:44:11,065 --> 00:44:13,859
Whoever is behind these bombings

693
00:44:13,942 --> 00:44:20,616
is giving Lily Cruz victory
on a silver platter!

694
00:44:20,949 --> 00:44:23,994
They're only boosting
that woman's resolve!

695
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:25,996
Really, Papa?

696
00:44:26,413 --> 00:44:28,415
You're not the one responsible
for those bombings?

697
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:32,586
I wasn't! Because if I'm going
to blow something up,

698
00:44:32,961 --> 00:44:35,005
I won't waste my time
with those buildings.

699
00:44:35,089 --> 00:44:37,466
I'd blow up Lily Cruz's head!

700
00:44:39,677 --> 00:44:43,889
Hold on, Papa. If you're not
the one behind that, then who?

701
00:44:44,515 --> 00:44:47,893
Does this mean Lily Cruz has a new enemy?

702
00:44:56,860 --> 00:44:58,320
Ma'am, we can still fix this,

703
00:44:58,404 --> 00:45:00,697
but we're going to get delayed
with the schedule.

704
00:45:01,156 --> 00:45:03,951
We need extra manpower to speed things up.

705
00:45:04,952 --> 00:45:07,204
All right. Let's hire a few more workers.

706
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:09,415
This area here was

707
00:45:09,498 --> 00:45:10,582
-[Diego] Lily.
-the most damaged.

708
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:13,627
The townspeople are here,
and they're all ready to help.

709
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:18,966
Good! Because investors
are committing 10 billion pesos

710
00:45:19,049 --> 00:45:21,844
for the rehabilitation of Aguas Realty,

711
00:45:22,094 --> 00:45:24,304
and they're offering to shoulder

712
00:45:24,388 --> 00:45:27,057
some of the victims' medical expenses.

713
00:45:27,933 --> 00:45:31,645
Lily, you have everyone's
full trust and support.

714
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:34,648
You're not alone in this fight, Miss Lily.

715
00:45:34,731 --> 00:45:36,275
We're right behind you! Right?

716
00:45:36,358 --> 00:45:38,902
-Yeah!
-We're with you.

717
00:45:38,986 --> 00:45:41,488
-Thank you, everyone.
-Excuse me. Move aside.

718
00:45:41,572 --> 00:45:45,451
Poor people, move, I need space.
Excuse me.

719
00:45:45,534 --> 00:45:46,535
-There she goes again.
-Excuse me.

720
00:45:46,618 --> 00:45:47,995
Hi, Lily Cruz.

721
00:45:48,078 --> 00:45:49,538
The Governor's office sent me here

722
00:45:49,621 --> 00:45:51,457
to show our support for your project.

723
00:45:51,540 --> 00:45:54,626
So, how are you, Lily?
Well, what can I say?

724
00:45:54,710 --> 00:45:56,044
That was one "explosive" surprise.

725
00:45:56,128 --> 00:45:58,046
You shook the whole world!

726
00:45:58,297 --> 00:45:59,965
Don't tell me the Ardientes

727
00:46:00,048 --> 00:46:01,758
didn't have anything
to do with those bombings.

728
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:03,886
Excuse me, Camia. Watch your mouth.

729
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:05,387
We don't know anything about that.

730
00:46:05,471 --> 00:46:07,973
In fact, I went here to know.

731
00:46:08,056 --> 00:46:10,559
I want to know who's responsible
for those bombings,

732
00:46:10,642 --> 00:46:12,769
so I can hug him or her,

733
00:46:12,853 --> 00:46:17,608
and then shake their hand,
and tell them, "Good job!"

734
00:46:18,859 --> 00:46:20,736
Well, this little guy
wants to know you better.

735
00:46:22,196 --> 00:46:23,197
Aren't you going to leave?

736
00:46:24,114 --> 00:46:25,407
Did that bother you?

737
00:46:25,491 --> 00:46:27,493
Why are you so worked up about this?

738
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:29,203
-Aren't you going to leave?!
-I'm going!

739
00:46:29,286 --> 00:46:30,787
-Get out of here!
-I'm leaving!

740
00:46:30,871 --> 00:46:32,498
-[man] Leave!
-Get out!

741
00:46:32,581 --> 00:46:33,707
[exasperated sigh]

742
00:46:36,543 --> 00:46:39,922
I don't believe the Ardientes
weren't involved!

743
00:46:40,005 --> 00:46:42,090
Emilia was just lying again.

744
00:46:43,175 --> 00:46:45,052
I'm sorry, Mom, but it's possible

745
00:46:45,135 --> 00:46:47,179
that she was telling the truth.

746
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:50,265
The Ardientes have been crippled.

747
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:53,143
They're incapable of carrying out

748
00:46:53,227 --> 00:46:54,436
simultaneous bombings.

749
00:46:54,895 --> 00:46:58,065
So, if they aren't behind it, who is?

750
00:46:59,107 --> 00:47:01,193
Who else could possibly go against you?

751
00:47:01,735 --> 00:47:03,028
My thoughts exactly.

752
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:06,698
The Ardientes are my only enemies.

753
00:47:07,366 --> 00:47:12,371
But I suspect that someone
is helping them.

754
00:47:14,873 --> 00:47:18,627
Someone who is capable
of a large-scale terror attack.

755
00:47:19,753 --> 00:47:21,922
I'll find out who they are.

756
00:47:34,977 --> 00:47:36,228
Are you all right?

757
00:47:41,024 --> 00:47:44,403
Diego, do you remember that woman
at the construction site?

758
00:47:44,820 --> 00:47:47,197
The one I asked you about?

759
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:48,991
Yes. Why?

760
00:47:51,285 --> 00:47:53,996
I didn't tell you earlier,
but I have a strong feeling

761
00:47:54,079 --> 00:47:56,290
that she may have something
to do with the bombings.

762
00:47:58,375 --> 00:48:00,252
Why didn't you tell that
to the investigator?

763
00:48:02,129 --> 00:48:05,465
We don't know who we're up against.

764
00:48:07,092 --> 00:48:10,220
At this point, we shouldn't trust anyone.

765
00:48:10,304 --> 00:48:13,432
So, I hope we can keep this conversation

766
00:48:13,515 --> 00:48:14,975
between the two of us for now.

767
00:48:16,727 --> 00:48:20,606
What's important now is
for me to find that woman.

768
00:48:21,815 --> 00:48:23,984
I believe she's our key to finding out

769
00:48:24,067 --> 00:48:25,944
who's behind the bombings.

770
00:48:28,196 --> 00:48:30,741
[suspenseful music playing]

771
00:48:38,206 --> 00:48:40,876
<i>Has our investment</i>
<i>in Aguas Realty been approved?</i>

772
00:48:40,959 --> 00:48:42,628
<i>They have to go through me.</i>

773
00:48:42,711 --> 00:48:44,963
[Paterno] <i>That Lily Cruz</i>
<i>is so full of herself!</i>

774
00:48:45,047 --> 00:48:46,173
<i>Blow them up.</i>

775
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:48,425
[Mr. Paterno] <i>I would like you to meet</i>
<i>Mrs. Mercedes' associate.</i>

776
00:48:48,508 --> 00:48:50,677
<i>You! Stop her!</i>

777
00:48:50,761 --> 00:48:52,054
[people clamoring]

778
00:48:52,137 --> 00:48:55,182
[reporter] <i>We're here at the</i>
<i>main office of Aguas Realty</i>

779
00:48:55,265 --> 00:48:58,852
<i>where an alleged</i>
<i>terrorist threat was reported.</i>

780
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:01,688
<i>Looks like karma is a bigger witch</i>

781
00:49:01,772 --> 00:49:03,231
<i>than you are, Miss Lily Cruz.</i>

782
00:49:03,315 --> 00:49:05,025
<i>Where's the bomb?!</i>

783
00:49:05,651 --> 00:49:09,863
[suspenseful music playing]

784
00:49:11,031 --> 00:49:13,700
[theme music playing]
